      "quick_win": false,
      "title": "Expose role-specific application result types",
      "body": "The page has to force both branches through assertions, including `unknown`, because `getApplications` returns a role-dependent payload without a discriminant in its type. Return an explicitly discriminated role/result union (or separate read actions) and narrow it before rendering. That keeps the secretariat projection contract checked whenever fields or permissions change.",
      "rule_ids": [],
      "guideline": null,
      "suggestion": null,
      "evidence": [
        "Premise: app/admin/solicitacoes/page.tsx:20-22 uses `applications as SecretariatApplicationSummary[]` and `applications as unknown as ...ApplicationSummary[]` → Improvement: compile-time checking will detect mismatches between the server projections and their role-specific clients → Fix: model `getApplications` as a discriminated union keyed by staff role, or split its role-specific reads.",
        "app/admin/_actions/admin-actions.ts:61-90 → the action selects different column sets conditionally by the authenticated role.",
        "app/admin/solicitacoes/page.tsx:19-23 → the same role branch is available to perform a typed union narrowing."
      ]
    },
